mantle rm216
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier full
written_for rm_ulla_rustham
title the second swatch
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=crafter
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk compares_colours_against_the_inside_of_a_wrist
likes smoked_eel whittling a_full_till summer_evenings
dislikes salt_wind stale_bread
fears promises_made_by_lamplight loose_batch_labels
hopes an_even_wash a_drawer_of_true_samples
topics work +0.5 lore +0.3 smalltalk +0.4 pastimes +0.3 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=instructions gossip=withheld refuse=exact tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# gives long, exact accounts of small visible differences, asks to see every sample twice, and uses a wrist as a private standard of comparison.

words
oath! = Shallow pan and purple water | Wool in the rinse again
saying! = Keep the second swatch | A shade changes its story at the door
sample = the second swatch | the folded sample
inside = the inside of my wrist | my pale wrist fur
dyewater = the coloured rinse | a pan of tint
selvedge = the woven edge | that close edge of cloth
reedpeg = a split reed peg | the hollow peg
shaving = a curled wood shaving | a thin curl of pearwood
stub = the square-ended stick | my nicked stick
packet = a wax-paper fold | the waxed packet
rindedge = a hard bread edge | that greyish crust
chiptray = a tray of chips | the little chip tray
threadtag = a doubled thread tag | the tagged end of the skein
nightblue = blue seen by lamplight | the blue of a covered flame
benchlight = sidelong light | light across the grain
tillnote = the good weight of coin | the settled chink in a drawer
eelpiece = the firm bit of smoked eel | that strip of brown eel
clothpin = a wooden clip | the plain bone clip
paleness = one degree less colour | a shade nearer white

any
opinion dole against 1 : Wages bought my first stool. I'd rather see a queue for stools with work to do at them.
opinion city for 2 : I couldn't have learned so many shades in a place with one hill and two roofs.
opinion festivals for 2 : Put a hundred different ribbons outdoors and every ribbon looks freshly made.
opinion merchants for 1 : Pay the keeper who remembers what you asked for after the coin lands in the drawer.
opinion road against 1 : A deep rut shakes a lid loose. The colour in the dust is proof of the cost of a road.
opinion strangers against 2 : An unfamiliar face gets daylight across a table before it gets an invitation indoors.
opinion watch for 1 : I'd sooner have a patrol within call than a shutter barred the whole afternoon.
opinion houses mixed 1 : A good commission pays many wages. A crest demanding the last word earns its own surcharge.
opinion drink mixed 1 : Wine and lamplight together can turn any colour lovely. Finish choosing before the second cup.

grown
line greet : Come into the better light, just there. | Welcome. I'd like a clear view of your expression.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : You have the advantage of a new face. Mine's in the light already. | Stand by that lighter patch till I have your outline.
line greet [self.working=yes] : Walk wide of that wet patch and you're welcome to look. | You'll find a clean standing place if you follow my elbow.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Clear edge of daylight at last. Good morning. | Daylight shows which edge is which. You came at a good hour.
line greet.return : Yes, I see you distinctly now. | #greet#. We can speak quite well across this distance.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : I'd know the voice with only half this light. | Your greeting arrives before its owner in this dim light.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : No need for the formal welcome. You've seen my untidy corners. | You've seen my face before I've had it quite in order.
line again.open : You saw me with the light falling the other way earlier. | Same wolf, different background. I recognise you.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Come look at a difference just big enough to argue over! | Your eye would come in handy. Step this way!
line farewell : Take a long look before you decide anything. | Off you go, then. I like a clean stopping place.
line farewell.return : I expect we'll come across each other in a different light. | I daresay we'll have new evidence to compare another time.
line react.news : Which part was observed and which part filled in? | I'd like the order of things as well as their colours.
line react.news.new : I'd have remembered a piece of news with that colour to it. | My recollection has nothing remotely that shade in it.
line react.news.known : Yes, I heard the substance. The edges seem to alter in every telling. | That bit comes out the same each time I hear it.
line react.news.doubt : A second account from a different doorway might persuade me. | Two mouths repeating one witness still make just one witness.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That's the sort of news I want delivered once, carefully. | That's a dark piece of news. No need to embroider it.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|work] : A bright thing to have heard with my own ears. | A bit of colour back in the town, then.
line answer.how : I can tell two near shades apart. My day's perfectly adequate. | My eyes agree with each other today. That's condition enough for good work.
line answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I'm halfway through the part that can't be left halfway. | My paws are engaged on different parts of one very awkward job.
line ask.how : What particular difficulty brought that crease to your forehead? | Is that a tired look or have I caught the shadow wrong?
line sympathise : Telling it once should suffice. I can attend the first time. | Take the chair facing away from traffic. I'll hear you better there.
line reassure : I can remember the order even when the words run away from you. | A proper account takes the breath it takes.
line decline : I'd need better particulars before I undertook any part of it. | I can't agree till somebody tells me exactly what's involved.
line accept_decline : Very well. I'll put the question back in its box. | I'll draw a line under that particular request.
line thank : You saw a detail I'd overlooked. I owe you for the sharp eye. | Your observation paid for itself very nicely.
line deflect_thanks : I wanted it done that way myself. We both gained. | You gave me something to look at. That's a return.
line preclose : I'd like to keep the last of this light for something small. | I need an uninterrupted moment to examine something.
line accept_preclose : We'll put a pin through the subject there. | A distinct ending suits me very well.
line ack : That's a shade clearer. | Well distinguished.
line give.advice : Keep one piece aside that hasn't been touched. Compare against that. | Turn the thing around before you blame one side.
line warn [world.bandits=near] : Have someone count the load at both ends of that road. | Take a written count with you. A raided load is difficult to describe from memory.
line again.open [pair.band=friends] : Back at a more interesting angle already.

scene wrist
when topic=smalltalk|pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I compare a bit of colour with #inside#. | I hold one paw over the other till only a strip of fur shows.
b[job=crafter] #turn : A standard you carry about in the weather? | Why only one strip to judge by?
b : Is that pale enough for the comparison? | Why make the strip narrow?
a@turn : Of course it varies. I can tell exactly how it's varying, which is the part that matters. | So I'm comparing touching edges. A wide gap lets my eye invent the difference.
a : It's familiar enough. I know how it'll look at noon and at dusk. | A whole pawful of pale makes anything beside it look dark.

scene matching
when topic=work self.job=crafter
does give.opinion / challenge / answer.detail / concede
a : I won't call two dyed pieces alike indoors. | One little blue strip ought to come free with a broad length of blue.
b : Even under a good lamp? | What's the scrap good for?
a : A lamp warms both. They look like cousins till daylight parts them. | Hold it by whatever you need to go with the length.
b : I'd sooner find that out at the door. | That would save carrying the whole roll about.

scene price_tags
when topic=prices self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A pretty tag can make a small price look suspicious. | I write price tags large enough to read across a table.
b : Better to use an ugly tag? | Afraid folk will ask?
a : Plain, if you please. Let the goods have the luxury. | I'd prefer a question about the goods. The figure needn't take up time.

scene split_peg
when topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can make #reedpeg# with one careful cut. | I like the second peg I cut better than the first.
b[job=crafter] #turn : And the grain has to run down the jaws? | Do you keep the first as a pattern?
b : Where do you start? | Is the first a trial?
a@turn : Precisely. Cross-grain makes a neat noise and two useless splinters. | I keep the best one. Very seldom the first.
a : At the fat end. Leave one joint whole or the thing becomes two sticks. | It tells me which way the grain's leaning. The next cut goes with it.

scene damp_voice
when topic=health here.weather=rain
does tell.complaint / reassure / assess
a : The damp lays hold of the middle of a sentence. I was about to finish one. | I can manage my own throat. It's the sentence I don't like losing.
b : Start at the last word you meant. | I caught the part about the peg.
a : An excellent suggestion. The last word was 'finished'. | Oh, good. That leaves only the length and the grain to explain.

scene washed
when topic=work self.job=crafter self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I wash #sample# before I promise a shade. | A bowl of rinse tells a buyer something the cloth doesn't.
b : Even if nobody's going to wash it? | How can water tell me anything?
a : Somebody always does, sooner or later. I like to meet that somebody first. | Watch what the first bowl takes away. Then decide which colour you've bought.

scene bread
when topic=food self.dislikes=stale_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can hear stale bread before I bite it. | If all that's left is #rindedge#, I ask for a bowl as well.
b : Does the crust talk? | A bowl of what?
a : The cut talks. Dry rasp all the way through if yesterday's well behind it. | Anything pleasant and wet. That crust has already proved its point.

scene fish_wrap
when topic=food self.likes=smoked_eel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I turn the wrapping back neatly from #eelpiece#. | There's a faint brass glint on eel skin that smoke brings out.
b : Saving the wrapper? | Does that make it tastier?
a : Saving my cuffs. The paper does its last useful work as a handle. | It makes me take my time before I taste it. That's near enough.

scene mother
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can sit easily with #self.mother# without putting my work on display. | I think of #self.mother# when a likeness is nearly right.
b : You'll show it to anyone else? | What does nearly right remind you of?
a : Not just anyone. It's a comfort to have one less judge in a room. | How much more I notice about a face that's familiar.

scene coins
when topic=prices|pastimes self.likes=a_full_till
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A drawer sounds different if the coins lie flat. | I push the little coins out of the corner before I count.
b : Fuller? | Afraid of missing one?
a : Shorter. Less room for a coin to strike another on its edge. | Afraid of counting the same bright rim on two different piles.

scene bay_air
when topic=weather here.weather=storm|overcast self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.complaint / give.advice / concede
a : Bay air leaves a pale whisker round every dark thing I own. | The first thing I taste on a windy day is salt.
b : Isn't the edge just where you want a pale line? | You could turn your muzzle uphill.
a : In a pattern, perhaps. I'll save that idea for a border. | For as long as the hill will consent to move ahead of me, certainly.

scene door_chain
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A chain at my door gives me a hand's width to look through. | I put my chair where a face at the door catches the light.
b[old] #turn : Could a caller wait while you eased the chain? | Does a chair by the sill give you a draught?
b : How long do you need to decide? | To study a visitor's expression?
a@turn : Anybody in too great a hurry for that can keep going. | I can close the window. Outside light still reaches a muzzle through a pane.
a : Long enough for a voice to say what it came for. | Precisely. A polite voice doesn't always bring pleased eyes.

scene off_colour
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A colour can look wrong with absolutely nothing wrong about it. | Put two greys side by side and one acquires a tint at once.
b : Wrong compared with what? | Which of the greys changes?
a : With yesterday's expectation. Eyes carry old accounts too. | Both, to my eye. Cover either and the survivor settles down.

scene night_blue
when topic=day here.time=night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : See how #nightblue# has nearly gone black? | I keep a pale thread beside any dark work in poor light.
b : Would it lighten at the window? | To guide your paw?
a : Tomorrow it would. Tonight there isn't much blue to borrow from the sky. | To warn my eye. If the pale goes yellow it's time to put the work aside.

scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does confide / react.self / assess
a : I'd let #self.friend# point out a fault while there's still time to mend it. | I like choosing a seat for #self.friend# by the window.
b : Pride takes a knock that way. | A good view?
a : Only a little knock. A public mistake knocks a good deal harder. | Good light. A view is a pleasant extra.

scene new_faces
when topic=newcomer
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : I'd have a new arrival say what brought a stranger through the gate. | A polite introduction can leave out nearly every interesting detail.
b : A tired traveller may only want supper. | Leave room for a second meeting.
a : After the meal, then. I'm quite prepared to wait for particulars. | A second meeting in daylight, and I'll hear you out.

scene festival
when topic=festival
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Give me an hour to watch the hems of festival clothes. | I can enjoy the ribbons before the dancing even starts.
b : Why the hems? | Are ribbons so much to look at?
a : Near the ground the colours borrow dust and the work of getting there. | Put ten pale ones together. You'll see more kinds of pale than you have words for.

scene ledger
when topic=work self.role=merchant self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I tuck a bit of the batch into the bill's fold. | Where two orders differ by one word I put a little mark in both margins.
b : Like a seal? | Why both?
a : Like a memory the keeper and buyer can hold together. | One mark means a surprise. Two marks tell me what I'm comparing.

scene two_hills
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At the bottom of these terraces you see far more red brick in reflection. | The colours on a hill change when you walk to its foot.
b : Reflected where? | Even on a clear day?
a : In windows higher up than their neighbours. The city keeps borrowing its own face. | Especially then. Look up and the eaves put a dark border round every roof.

scene low_trade
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When orders thin, buyers ask for smaller parcels and stay talking longer. | I let a customer take #sample# away before deciding on the length.
b : Do you mind the talk? | In a lean spell?
a : No. It tells me which small things might be wanted next. | That's when a wrong choice bites deepest.

scene wagons
when topic=caravan world.wagons=raided
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : After a raid I want a list of what's actually known missing. | A robbed wagon starts a fine trade in guesses.
b : Who keeps such a list? | Why would a guess be worth anything?
a : Ask the ones who loaded it. The taproom had no paw in the packing. | Because a frightened buyer might pay for it. Reason enough to keep quiet.

scene inventory
when topic=work self.job=crafter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A label tied round a wet skein dries too tight. | I leave long tails on #threadtag#.
b : How loose do you leave it? | Easier to catch?
a : Loose enough for a fingertip. The colour must get under the binding. | Easier to find again when the whole basket's the colour of the tag.

scene wood_test
when topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm making a row of little wooden tongues. | A carving needn't look like an animal to earn its place.
b : For a toy? | What do you carve instead?
a : For laying out colours. Wood keeps its opinion when the cloth shifts. | A thin stick that bends and springs back. I like a shape that does something.

scene travel_fold
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : On a journey I pack the palest thing in the middle. | When I tie a travelling bundle the knot goes underneath a fold.
b : What good's the clean thing in the middle? | Won't that be awkward?
a : When everything else is dusty it shows how much so. | For me, a little. For a curious passing paw, rather more.

scene health
when topic=health
does confide / react.self / assess
a : I sometimes drink a little water as much for the silence as the drink. | When my voice catches, I pick up whatever I'm holding and turn it round.
b : It gives you a moment. | To cover it?
a : Yes. Drinking looks quite deliberate to a visitor. | To give us both another subject while I get my breath.

scene questions
when topic=smalltalk|dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like one question on a card at the door before a caller comes through. | I once dreamed everybody's sleeves had labels saying why they'd come.
b : What's the question? | Would you read them all?
a : I'd ask whether to fetch my purse, my tools or a chair. | Every one. Then I woke and was rather glad nobody could read mine.

scene blue_edge
when topic=season here.season=summer here.time=dusk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Summer evenings give a colour three chances to change before dark. | I like a long dusk because I don't have to carry two samples far.
b : Three chances? | Why two?
a : First the sun goes. Then the pink goes. Finally my patience goes. | One at the window and one by the wall. Even a short arm can make the comparison.

scene news_held
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I heard that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's the account, stripped of trimming. | Here's the word in town: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : Did it have much trimming? | You'll swear to that?
a : More than I cared to repeat. Ask about what went into the dye, not what stained the rag. | I'll swear it's the word in town. I can be remarkably particular about oaths.

scene glove
when topic=home|pastimes
does offer / accept / assess
a : Take these two scraps over by the door. | Here, cup the ends of the cloth in both paws.
b : All right. They look much closer together now. | Darker in the hollow, isn't it?
a : And you've changed nothing but where you stand. Good to remember in an argument. | Yes. How deep the shadow goes teaches twice as much as a glance at the surface.

scene chip_labels
when topic=lore|work self.job=crafter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I label a sample at the end that's least interesting. | I put my mark opposite the selvedge when cloth is cut for keeping.
b : A label distracts from the shade? | Can you find your edge afterwards?
a : Yes. Your eye reads the label first and sees what the letters promised. | The selvedge holds together. My cut edge needs thread. You could feel that in the dark.

story pink_board [topic=memories self.age>=22]
  : Once I wiped a red pan with an old board scraping. That little shaving came up a pink I'd been looking for all week.
  : It dried by the sill while I tried the same on cloth. The cloth went grey.
  b : Did you keep the wood?
  : Yes. It's a very instructive piece of pink disappointment.

story closed_sample [topic=work self.job=crafter]
  : An order once came with a little folded bit of dyed yarn.
  : I worked all day to match the outside. The inside turned out to be another colour altogether.
  b : Which did the buyer mean?
  : The inside. Said the outside had faded. Ever since, I open a fold before I open my mouth.

story eel_mistake [topic=food self.likes=smoked_eel]
  : I once unwrapped supper at my bench and dipped a strip into my rinse water without thinking.
  : My sample thread was safe and dry in the bread beside it.
  b : Did you try eating the thread?
  : No. I paid closer attention to my second supper.

story chip_bird [topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling]
  : I cut one shaving so thin the slightest breath made it lift like a wing.
  : I spent an hour carving the bird to go behind that wing.
  b : Was the bird a likeness?
  : Of a lump of old wood, exactly. I kept the wing by itself.

story the_stall [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : As a young wolf I once spent a whole market day listening to a seller describe a handsome violet.
  : At closing time the awning came down. Filtered through the awning, an ordinary grey had looked magnificent.
  b : Was there a quarrel?
  : One very quiet sale. I bought the awning.

rule @wet_label
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=crafter
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Labels well clear of that rinse, please. | Let the split tag hang loose till the colour takes.

rule @trade
when concept=bark working=yes self.role=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Take the samples over to the doorway! | Compare them edge to edge before you choose.

rule @tidy
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=crafter
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Clean reed for the palest test. | Keep yesterday's stirring stick out of this pan.

rule @summer
when concept=bark here.season=summer here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A little more good light in that corner! | Turn the tray before the last pink goes.

rule @coins
when concept=bark self.likes=a_full_till
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Lay the coins flat where both can count. | No stacking small coin under large.

rule @whittle
when concept=bark self.likes=whittling
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep the curl you've pared away! | That little shaving's my best bit yet.

dlg resident.hub : Ask your first question. We'll give it a thorough airing before the second.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I had the right of your name before you spoke.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : A shade late for colours, an excellent time for particulars.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : You can make your business plain quite well from there.
dlg resident.job [self.job=crafter] : I keep a piece to compare with every finished batch. Want to see the differences?
dlg resident.job : I set two things alongside and look for what might have changed.
dlg resident.business [business=steady] : Steady orders give me time to check the little differences.
dlg resident.business [business=failing] : Too many specimens, too few orders. I'm counting carefully.
dlg resident.business [business=thriving] : Busy enough to pay for fresh light before sunrise and after dusk.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : I heard this much, in these words. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : No whispers worth taking out and showing you today.
dlg resident.bye : Remember which side was facing the light.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=open] : Stand close enough to compare goods, please. I can move them for you.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : My shelf stands empty. Show me anything you've brought.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=open topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, you'll remember the best light falls over here.
dlg shop.prices : #shop_dear# No asking figure of mine will change between this shelf and that door.
dlg shop.bye : Keep the wrapping folded till you mean to open it.

graft resident.hub
choice Why hold things to your wrist? -> wrist_light
node wrist_light
say I know what shade the fur is, even before I look at it. The other thing is what I'm trying to see.
mood keen
choice Would my own wrist do? -> wrist_own
choice I'm satisfied. -> hub
node wrist_own
say Certainly. Look at it for a moment on its own. Few wolves seem acquainted with that patch of their own fur.
choice Look at your wrist. -> hub
choice Take your leave. -> bye

graft shop.greet
choice May I take the two samples to the door? [self.job=crafter] -> show_samples
node show_samples
say By all means. First hold both to the light. Now fold one over the other and see how much colour goes missing in the fold.
mood formal
choice What if I like the folded shade? -> double_thickness
choice Set the samples down. -> greet
node double_thickness
say Then what you want is a double thickness. Buying a darker colour saves cloth but it won't do quite the same thing.
choice Look over the wares. -> greet
choice Leave the samples here. -> bye
